PATCH 624: preserve the original default mixer completion callback ABI (board:0003).

CALL [157b/157f/1583] reaches the original 2294 RET callback. It has no C
arguments or return value. The source trace at 13257 proves channel two's
rollover CALL/RET preserves EAX/ECX/EDX/EBX/EBP/ESI/EDI and pops four bytes
from ESP. The rollover routine separately saves/restores EAX. In particular,
ECX keeps the new pitch (zero for the original silence sample), while EDX
keeps the preceding partial sample. Do not overwrite either with Ghidra's
uninitialized extraout locals after a call. The same original default RET
vector is installed in all three channel slots.

Call the resolved actual void(void) function and retain the live C values.
The old int-returning call type traps on WASM; native proceeds but emits
unequal mixed bytes. The paging-aware paired original buffer/state fixture
and complete independent trace prove one rollover, one default RET callback
and 1024 stores. Both original 16000-ms captures retain every frame/PCM byte.
The regression binds the actual translated 2294 body, counts calls, compares
all one-MiB module bytes, every mixed byte and the untouched DMA half.
No callback is stubbed or skipped. Register-mutating custom callback ABIs,
other channel-switch variants, IRQ/device cadence and elapsed work remain
unproved; this patch adds no fixed delay or guessed register value.
